.TH DF 1 "September 2026" "mitos-utils 0.1.0" "MITOS User Commands"
.SH NAME
df \- report file system disk space usage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B df
[\fIPATH\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Report size, used, and available space for the filesystem containing each PATH (the current directory by default).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
Every mitos-utils command additionally accepts \fB\-\-help\fR (print a usage line and exit) and \fB\-\-version\fR. Commands that take file/path arguments also accept \fB\-\-\fR to mark the end of options, so a file literally named e.g. \fB\-oddfile\fR can still be referenced.
.SH NOTES
Linux only, via statvfs(2); the "Filesystem" source-device column is not populated (statvfs doesn't expose the device name). See mitos-utils-compat(7) for the FFI verification notes.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if any PATH's filesystem info could not be read.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mitos\-box (1),
.BR mitos\-utils\-compat (7),
.BR mitos\-utils\-integration (7)
